<text>
pair_size = pfkey_sockaddr_pair_size(mp->old_family);
if (!pair_size)
	return -EINVAL;
size_pol += sizeof(struct sadb_x_ipsecrequest) + pair_size;

pair_size = pfkey_sockaddr_pair_size(mp->new_family);
if (!pair_size)
	return -EINVAL;
size_pol += sizeof(struct sadb_x_ipsecrequest) + pair_size;
</text>
<text>
int set_ipsecrequest(..., sa_family_t family, ...)
</text>
Reason:
The fix adds explicit validation of each family in `pfkey_send_migrate()` by capturing the return value of `pfkey_sockaddr_pair_size()` and returning `-EINVAL` if it is zero. This ensures that only valid families are used for size calculations, preventing underallocation of the skb. The type of the `family` parameter in `set_ipsecrequest()` is changed from `uint8_t` to `sa_family_t`, which is large enough to hold all valid address families (e.g., `AF_INET6` = 10) without truncation. This corrects the size calculations inside `set_ipsecrequest()` and eliminates the mismatch that led to the buffer overflow.

